# Atlas Button — a Skia Atlas of 50x40 tiny squares (per-sprite RSXform computed
# in a worklet from the press progress) that bloom outward from the centre while
# the button is held; the React logo lifts and a "React Native" label fades in;
# releasing logs "Button pressed".
# What this test covers: a quick tap (log), a long hold (full bloom, 1200ms
# spring) then release, rapid taps reversing the spring mid-bloom, a hold that
# drags sideways off the button, and taps near the canvas corners (250x200 canvas).
# expect-log: Button pressed
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/atlas-button"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 45000
# Warm-up touch on the status bar: the first touch of a test can be lost while
# the XCTest runner attaches.
press 330 20
wait 500
wait 1500
press 201 437
wait 1500
longpress 201 437 3000
wait 2000
press 201 437 --count 8 --interval-ms 100
wait 2000
gesture pan 201 437 170 0 1500
wait 2000
# Corners of the 250x200 canvas (x 76..326, y 337..537).
press 85 345
wait 800
press 318 530
wait 800
longpress 201 437 800
wait 2000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 15000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
